{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The flat requirement that the document \"must be signed by all students\" cannot be squared with c003-c004, which contemplate that a minor student may lack legal competency to sign and require a parent to sign on the minor's behalf. It is left open whether a minor's own signature has any binding effect or is a mere formality.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The definitional carve-out \"unless indicated otherwise\" sets no standard for when the document has so indicated, and no provision is expressly flagged as adult-only or minor-only. Whether obligations such as the release and indemnity apply to a minor as \"Student\" therefore turns on an undefined qualifier.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The parent's signature is described only \"as evidence of Parent's acknowledgment and agreement,\" leaving ambiguous whether the parent thereby becomes a contracting party bound personally and whether the parent can bind the minor's own claims. \"(under 18 years of age in most states)\" further leaves the triggering age indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The duty to \"determine the age of legal competency to sign contracts\" is imposed on the student and parent with no standard, no consequence for getting it wrong, and no statement of what happens if the residence state's age differs from the \"under 18\" figure used in c003. The provision states an obligation whose breach and effect are unspecified.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The activity list is introduced by \"include, among others,\" so the enumerated activities do not bound what counts as a NOLS activity. That open catch-all controls the reach of the release in c044, which applies to \"an activity of NOLS.\"", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Inherent risks\" is defined by reference to risks that \"cannot be eliminated without destroying the unique character of the activities,\" a phrase with no ascertainable boundary. That definition determines the scope of the assumption in c042 and the negligence line drawn in c046.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c014", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c015", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c016", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c017", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c018", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c019", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Travel is described as by the listed conveyances \"and by other means,\" and the terrain list is prefaced by \"including,\" so neither enumeration limits anything. A dispute over whether a particular mode of travel (e.g. contractor-driven vehicles) was disclosed turns on this open catch-all.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.11}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c020", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The sentence as it appears begins with unintelligible characters and has no stated subject for the verb \"include,\" so the risks enumerated have no identified antecedent. A reader must supply \"travel risks\" from the preceding bullet to give the sentence meaning.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c021", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Forces of nature, including weather which may change to extreme conditions\" is a catch-all appended to a specific list of hazards, with no boundary on what else it captures. Whether an unlisted hazard was a disclosed risk depends on this open-ended term.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.09}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c022", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Other mild or serious conditions\" is a residual catch-all following a specific list of illnesses, which effectively swallows the enumeration. Its breadth determines what injuries count as disclosed for purposes of the assumption of risk in c042.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.09}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c023", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c024", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c025", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"On most NOLS courses\" and \"at times during the day\" leave it undetermined whether unsupervised travel was disclosed for this student's particular course. Whether the risk was in fact assumed under c042 turns on that indefinite qualifier.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.13}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c026", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Free\" time is placed in scare quotes and never defined, yet it is the operative trigger for the disclaimers in c027 and c028. Whether an interval during the course counts as \"free\" time is left entirely open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c027", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The disclaimer covers free time \"before and after their course\" although c026 describes free time \"before, during and after\"; by expressio unius NOLS retains responsibility for free time during the course. The omission of \"during\" is the words needing repair.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c028", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This sentence disclaims responsibility for staff conduct in \"these free time activities\" generally, which cannot be squared with c027's narrower disclaimer limited to free time before and after the course. The two cannot both be given effect as to in-course free time.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c029", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Cannot continually monitor\" is phrased as a statement of fact rather than a disclaimer of duty, leaving unclear whether it limits NOLS's supervisory obligations at all. The degree of monitoring NOLS does undertake is nowhere specified.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c030", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Students must \"accept responsibility for themselves and others,\" a phrase that does not say whether it imposes mere self-care or a legal liability for injuries to other people. Read with the indemnity in c045 it could be argued to create financial responsibility for third-party harm.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c031", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c032", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c033", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Generally consistent with customs and standards used in the United States\" is an affirmative representation about foreign field practices with no ascertainable content and an escape word (\"generally\"). It sits inside a risk-disclosure passage yet reads as a standard-of-care promise.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c034", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c035", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Certain tasks, including, for example, transportation\" gives one illustration and no boundary, so the class of contractor-performed tasks is undefined. That open class fixes the reach of the contractor disclaimer in c036.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c036", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The disclaimer for contractors' acts cannot readily be squared with c044, which releases NOLS's \"agents\" as Released Parties without mentioning contractors, leaving unclear whether a contractor is inside or outside the released group. It also appears only in the descriptive risk bullets rather than in the operative release.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c037", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The acknowledgment incorporates the Catalog \"and/or\" the NOLS website without identifying an edition or date, so what the student is agreeing he has read is indeterminate. Website content can change unilaterally after signature.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c038", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"And other material provided by NOLS describing or related to my program\" is an unbounded catch-all appended to three named documents. Whether an unnamed brochure or e-mail is part of the acknowledged information is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c039", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The clause states only that staff \"has been available\" to explain the activities and risks, not that any explanation was in fact given or received. Whether this acknowledgment forecloses a claim of inadequate disclosure is ambiguous on its own words.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c040", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The acknowledgment that the risk description \"is not complete\" and extends to \"unknown or unanticipated\" risks is difficult to square with c007, which defines inherent risks by their connection to the unique character of the activities. Read together it is unclear whether unknown risks are assumed as \"inherent\" or only under the separate all-risks clause c043.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
  ]}
]}

